  "year": 1996,
  "authority": "Ukrainian Legal Terminology Commission, Decision No. 9 of 19.04.1996",
  "description": "Official Ukrainian–English system of Decision No. 9 of the Ukrainian Legal Terminology Commission (19.04.1996), binding for names in legislative and official acts until the 2010 resolution: like KMU 2010 but Щ→SCH and Ь→’.",
  "sources": [
    "https://web.archive.org/web/20080926111427/http://www.rada.gov.ua/translit",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanization_of_Ukrainian",
    "https://github.com/interscript/maps/blob/main/maps/ua-ukr-Cyrl-Latn-1996.isc"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Samples are the examples of the 1996 table (two misprints in the source, Ніжин → 'Nizhin' and Крюківка → 'Krukivka', are left out).",
    "The table gives ‘ for Ь (examples Rus’, L’viv, rendered here as ’ U+2019) and “ for the apostrophe, but its own example Знам’янка → Znamianka omits the apostrophe and the commentary allows omitting both marks; this scheme omits the apostrophe and keeps ’ for Ь. Wikipedia lists ʼ for Ь and ˮ for the apostrophe.",
    "The commentary also allows simplifying doubled letters (Zaporizhzhia → Zaporizhia); not applied.",
    "The 2004 passport practice listed on Wikipedia (variants g/h, zh/j, v/w, k/c; Ь → ʹ) is too ambiguous to encode as a separate scheme."
  ],
  "alphabet": "абвгґдеєжзиіїйклмнопрстуфхцчшщьюя",
